d  become wonder woman herself  her triumph is short-lived however as  the flash also travels back in time to  set things right  while there have technically been four  cheaters the honest truth is that there  are only two of real significance to the  comics  but it's still worth taking a moment to  find out more about the awesome  debbie domain is priscilla rich's niece  and heir to her fortune  ambivalent about her own wealth debbie  becomes an ecological activist and even  makes friends with wonder woman  after encountering the amazon at sea  unfortunately she's soon kidnapped by  agents of cobra and a regimen of torture  and brainwashing  turns her into an agent of evil she  never appeared in a wonder woman story  after her introduction  although she did turn up as a villain in  various other stories  published over the next few years  including crisis on infinite  earth the story that would ultimately  erase her from continuity  sebastian balasteros is an argentine  businessman  and lover of another wonder woman foe  the immortal sorceress cersei  in a 2001 storyline he is able to  convince  urz khataga the god who empowers cheetah  to take the cheetah's powers from  barbara and minerva  and give them to him instead sebastian  is ultimately no match for barbara and  however  unable to access the cheetah's powers  she instead steals the powers of one of  the furies of greek myth  and ultimately kills balosteros giving  his blood to urge kataga as an offering  in exchange for becoming cheater once  more  when barbara minerva was first  introduced in 1987 she was depicted as a  duplicitous woman  who feigns friendship with wonder woman  in an attempt to steal her magic lasso  when dc revised won the woman's  continuity in 2016  as part of dc rebirth however she was  made into a far more likable character  they also tied her origin more closely  to wonder womans  cementing them as fated arch nemesis in  the current continuity  barbara and minerva is a brilliant  ar